WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
This recorded proof of concept asks which version of a fictional rule applies. Every example uses fixed responses.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The local edition replays the language steps, then resolves evidence and checks citations in code.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:22.000
In the North, provision 3.A.6 requires inclusion by the beginning of the first full calendar month.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
On the same date in the South, the earlier edition still applies. Its deadline is the second full calendar month.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Release 1 references a missing ruling. The verifier flags the gap and returns the case for review.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The proposed change adds that ruling. The preview identifies cases whose evidence would change.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:52.000
After approval, the same question cites the new ruling and its conditional exception.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A separate amendment changes a definition. The register identifies when an earlier issued answer expires.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:07.000
All thirteen recorded layer cases met their authored expectations. The baseline received different inputs.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Citation checks cover the selected evidence. Interpreting the rule and finding missing knowledge still require judgment.

